      "year": 2020,
      "abstract": "The individual and ethnic differences of drug effects are very important issues in clinical drug therapy. They may be caused by genetic variations which mainly come from polymorphisms of genes encoding metabolic enzymes, transporters and drug targets that affect the in vivo pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamics of drugs. With the development and huge successes of HGP project, one of its major applications is emerge of a new research area of pharmacogenomics, which is used in standardization and individualization of drug therapy. In order to fulfill its goal, precision medicine is the key to solve the problem.",
